        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Netanyahu fails to address Israel’s failure to achieve war goals in Iran Middle East Issued on: 09/04/2026 - 07:50 Reporting from Jerusalem, FRANCE 24’s Noga Tarnopolsky says that when Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu finally made a statement on the US-Iran ceasefire, he failed to “address the fact that Israel has not achieved any of its stated war goals, which included regime change in Iran, the destruction of Iran's ability to launch and to produce ballistic missiles” and eliminate the nuclear threat. At least 182 killed as Israel strikes central Beirut after saying Iran truce doesn't apply there 08/04/2026 Middle East 'Pakistani military calling the shots: Has connections with IRCG, very good relationship with Trump' 08/04/2026 Middle East US-Iran truce: ‘Sensitive behind-the-scenes conversations’ paved way for Pakistan-brokered ceasefire 08/04/2026 Middle East Trump administration's claims of victory in Iran 'really quite hollow', analyst says 08/04/2026 Middle East Netanyahu says Israel ready to 'return to battle at any moment' against Iran 08/04/2026 Middle East Iran continues to target Gulf countries despite ceasefire announcement 08/04/2026 Middle East Iran closes Strait of Hormuz again as Israel pounds Lebanon, air defense systems go off in Tehran 08/04/2026 Middle East Israel's attacks on Beirut 'much bigger than anything we've seen in this war or the previous one' 08/04/2026 Middle East 'Unlawful' war on Iran: 'Use of force by the United States never justified' 08/04/2026 Middle East"
